<title>USA: Substance Abuse revises U.S. Drug offer.</title>
<headline>Substance Abuse revises U.S. Drug offer.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Substance Abuse Technologies Inc said on Monday it would revise its proposed offer to acquire the remaining outstanding shares of U.S. Drug Testing.</p>
<p>Under the revised offer, Substance Abuse said it would exchange Substance Abuse shares valued at $2.625 for each outstanding U.S. Drug share which it did not already hold.</p>
<p>&quot;Our board felt the need to restructure our offer of February 1996 because of the greater expenditures and time we now estimate for bringing U.S. Drug's products to market,&quot; Substance Abuse Chairman Robert Stutman said.</p>
</text>
